age":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"227 Lonsmount Dr","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"227 Lonsmount Dr, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Clay Buddies Pottery And Social Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/clay-buddies-pottery-and-social-club/"},"performer":"Clay Buddies Pottery And Social Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Day Trip to Niagara Falls with Hiking 🌿💧","url":"https://www.meetup.com/catholic-hang-out-social-group/events/316671411/","description":"Day Trip to Niagara Falls with Hiking 🌿💧\n\nJoin the Shalom Catholic Community for a day of fresh air, nature, and good company as we head to Niagara Falls for a hike and a picnic!\n\nWe'll walk scenic trails along the Niagara Gorge, enjoy the view of the falls, and share a picnic lunch together. It's a great chance to take a break from the city, meet new people, and enjoy the fall colours before the cold weather arrives. Everyone is welcome, whether you're part of the community or joining us for the first time.\n\n📅 When: Saturday, October 3\n🕗 Departure: 8:00 AM from Toronto, [meeting point]\n🚗 Transportation: Carpooling available\n💵 Cost: $30.00 [e-transfer: economatotoronto@comshalom.org]\n📝 Registration: Required by Tuesday, September 29\n\nWhat to bring:\n\nYour own light lunch\nSomething to share for the group picnic\nComfortable walking shoes and weather-appropriate clothing\nWater bottle and sunscreen\n\nSpots in the carpool are limited, so please register early to save your seat!\ni\n📞 Questions? Contact us at 647 222 9875\n\n📸 Follow us on Instagram: @shalomtoronto\n\nWe can't wait to spend the day with you! 🙌","startDate":"2026-10-03T12:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Niagara Falls","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"QC","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"Niagara falls, Toronto, QC"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Catholic Hang-out / Social Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/catholic-hang-out-social-group/"},"performer":"Catholic Hang-out / Social Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Yogasanas: Mind-Body Alignment (Isha Hatha Yoga) Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/isha-yoga-toronto-free-meditation-classes/events/316693725/","description":"Click [here](https://innerengineering.sadhguru.org/toronto) to register\n\nYogasanas\n\nThe word asana literally means a posture. Out of the innumerable asanas a body can assume, 84 have been identified as Yogasanas, through which one can transform the body and mind into a possibility for ultimate well-being. Yogasanas are not exercises, but rather very subtle processes to manipulate one’s energy in a particular direction.\n\nIn an untrained state, the human body is a constant manifestation of various levels of compulsiveness. By consciously forming the body into a certain posture, one creates a conducive passage for energy flow that can elevate one’s consciousness. Yogasanas are a way of aligning the inner system and adjusting it to the celestial geometry, thereby becoming in sync with the existence and naturally achieving a chemistry of healthfulness, joyfulness, blissfulness, and above all, balance.\n\nThe practice of Yogasanas provides countless benefits including:\n\n* Relief of chronic health conditions\n* Evolution of body and mind towards a higher possibility\n* Stabilization of the body, mind, and energy system\n* Deceleration of the aging process\n\nThis is a paid program.\n\nProgram fee: CAD 300\n\nSaturday, October 3rd, 8:00 AM - 11:30 AM\nSaturday, October 3rd, 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM\nSunday, October 4th, 8:00 AM - 11:30 AM\nSunday, October 4th, 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM\n\nFor ages 18 and above, no prior knowledge of yoga is required.","startDate":"2026-10-03T12:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"5825 Dixie Rd","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"5825 Dixie Rd, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Inner Engineering Toronto (Isha Yoga & Meditation Classes)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/isha-yoga-toronto-free-meditation-classes/"},"performer":"Inner Engineering Toronto (Isha Yoga & Meditation Classes)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Fall Migration Birding in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/316386951/","description":"**Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our website.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fall-birding-26)**\n\n**Toronto has some hidden natural gems, and October is when it puts on its best show.**\n\nJoin our guide Pedro Hernandez of[ Outdoor Commute](https://www.instagram.com/outdoor.commute/) for a beginner-friendly birdwatching walk through the unique Tommy Thompson Park. You do not need to know a warbler from a wren, but you probably will when the day is done. This walk is built for people who are simply curious about the birds sharing our skyline.\n\nWe’ll move slowly and stop often, learning how to identify species by shape, colour, and call, how to actually use a pair of binoculars (yours to borrow for the day), and how to make sense of field guides and birding apps you can keep using long after the trip ends.\n\nOctober is peak Fall migration in the city, with so many different birds to spot. Depending on conditions, we might spot warblers, sparrows, and thrushes moving through, along with waterfowl like northern shovelers and gadwalls resting on the water. Year-round residents including red-tailed hawks, black-capped chickadees, and northern cardinals tend to make an appearance too.\n\n**Please note that binoculars are included in the cost of the adventure and that, due to the Toronto location, transportation is not offered.**\n\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or provide feedback, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n\n**Highlights**\n**Fall Migration:** October is one of the best windows of the year to bird at the Spit, with local species and southbound migrants both moving through the park at once.\n**Professional Birder:** Pedro founded the popular birding account[ Outdoor Commute](https://www.instagram.com/outdoor.commute/) and brings a genuine, patient teaching style\n**Binoculars Included:** Every participant gets a pair of high-quality NOCS binoculars for the walk\n\n**Event cost: $60+HST (for explorer members). Register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fall-birding-26)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***","startDate":"2026-10-03T12:20:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":", Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/"},"performer":"Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":" Doors Open Brampton Road Trip — Heritage, History & Hidden Gems! $20","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316747277/","description":"# Doors Open Brampton Road Trip — Heritage, History & Hidden Gems!\n\n**Saturday, October 3, 2026**\n\nReady to explore Brampton from a whole new perspective? Join us for a Saturday road trip to[ ](https://www.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/brampton)**[Doors Open Brampton](https://www.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/brampton)**[, ](https://www.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/brampton)where historic buildings, museums, heritage sites and other interesting spaces open their doors to the public.\n\n### 🚗 The Road Trip\n\nWe'll meet **outside Christie Station at 8:30 AM** and travel together in a **Kia Soul equipped with SiriusXM radio**. 🎶\nWe'll head to Brampton for a day of exploring, with a focus on the downtown area so we can walk between several locations.\n\n### 💵 COST: $20\n\nThere is a **$20 charge for this event**.\nYour $20 covers:\n\n* 🚗 Round-trip transportation from Toronto to Brampton\n* ⛽ Fuel\n* 🔧 Other car operating expenses\n\n**Doors Open Brampton itself is free** — the $20 is strictly to cover the cost of transportation and operating the vehicle.\n\n### ⚠️ VERY LIMITED SPOTS!\n\nThis is a **very limited-capacity road trip**, so if you're interested, **sign up quickly!**\nTo lock in your spot, please send a **$20 e-transfer to:**\nnicolasbello@yahoo.com\n\n**Your spot is not confirmed until the $20 e-transfer has been received.**\n\n### 🏛️ [Exploring Brampton](https://www.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/brampton)\n\nWe'll focus on the downtown area and visit as many interesting Doors Open locations as we can within our limited time.\nPossible stops include:\n**📍 Brampton Downtown Heritage Walk**\nExplore Brampton's history, architecture and stories from the city's past.\n**📍 Alderlea**\nA beautifully preserved **1867 Italianate villa** overlooking Gage Park.\n**📍 Peel Art Gallery, Museum & Archives (PAMA)**\nExplore exhibitions, museum spaces and special Doors Open programming.\n**📍 Brampton Library – Four Corners Branch**\nCheck out this downtown location and its local-history resources.\nWe'll add other participating Doors Open locations as time permits.\n\n### ⏰ IMPORTANT TIMING\n\n**8:30 AM** — Meet outside Christie Station\n**8:30 AM** — Depart Toronto\n**10:00 AM** — Doors Open Brampton begins\n**10:00 AM–3:00 PM** — Explore Brampton\n**3:00 PM SHARP** — Depart Brampton for Toronto\n\n⚠️ **The 3 PM departure is firm!**\nNick has a **Nuit Blanche volunteer shift in Toronto**, so we absolutely need to leave Brampton at **3:00 PM sharp**.\nThat gives us roughly five hours to explore, so we'll keep things moving and make the most of our time.\n\n### 🎶 THE RIDE\n\nTravel in a **Kia Soul with SiriusXM radio**, good conversation and hopefully some great fall weather.\nThe ride there and back is part of the fun!\n\n### 👟 WHAT TO BRING\n\n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* Weather-appropriate clothing\n* Water\n* Camera/phone\n* Money for lunch, coffee or snacks\n* Your curiosity!\n\n**Rain or shine — we're going!**\n\n### 📌 MEETING POINT\n\n**Outside Christie Station**\n**8:30 AM SHARP**\nPlease arrive a few minutes early so we can leave on time.\n\n### 💰 RESERVE YOUR SPOT\n\n**$20 per person**\n📧 Send your **$20 e-transfer to** nicolasbello@yahoo.com to lock in your spot.\n🚨 **VERY LIMITED SPOTS AVAILABLE — SIGN UP FAST IF YOU'RE INTERESTED!**\n\nCome explore Brampton's history, architecture and hidden gems with us! 🏛️🚗","startDate":"2026-10-03T12:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Christie Station Labyrinth","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Christie, 5 Christie St, Toronto, ON M6G 3B1, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"3 Hrs Saturday Morning Feather Birdies Badminton","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gta-badminton-meetup/events/316638258/","description":"**Event Cost :** **$15** per person. (cash only) More then one brand new **Feather Birdies** per person to be supplied by event host.\n**Racquets :** Bring your own racquet. Rentals are available at the club if needed.\n**Shoes :** Please bring indoor gym shoes and change into them at the club before entering the courts.\n**Attention !!! please let us know at least 48 hours (Thursday@3PM) in advance if you or your guest can’t make it. This gives those on the waitlist a chance to join! Please note that \"no-shows\" or late cancellations are tracked; even a single occurrence may result in removal from the group to ensure active participation. Thanks for your cooperation!**","startDate":"2026-10-03T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Tiger badminton","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Markham","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"7755 warden ave, Unit 7, Markham, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto-GTA Badminton Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gta-badminton-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto-GTA Badminton Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Community Wim Hof practice","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-wim-hof-method-meetup-group/events/316539050/","description":"It's better when we're together. Come and experience the power of the WHM with a wonderful group of people. We breathe, we go into the cold and we teach our bodies to heat up properly. We develop resilience and the mindset to use these powerful healing tools over and over again, all year round. This gathering is fully guided by Wim Hof instructor Steve Beattie.\n\nIf you are new to this, come on down, enjoy the support and practice in a safe way with us. If you already have a WHM practice this meetup is a great way to take it to the next level, and make lots of new friends.\n\nThere will be a fire, snacks and drinks shared by other attendees. We have been doing this 6 for years!\n\n**What to bring?**\n\n* Yoga mat\n* Weather-appropriate clothing (better to dress too warm!)\n* Bathing suite, towel\n* Water shoes (optional)\n\nIn extreme weather being prepared is very important. Especially if it's your first time, please read up on how to come prepared [here.](https://www.breathinginnature.com/wim-hof-method-meetup/)\n\nLearn more about our Wim Hof meetups, workshops, breath classes, wilderness trips, medicine work and special events at **[Breathing in Nature](https://breathinginnature.com/)**.\n\nJoin the \"**[Wim Hof Toronto](https://www.facebook.com/groups/1714218015474146/)**\" group on Facebook to see all of our local events.\n\nThis is a free event made possible by our Gift Economy. You can learn more about the Gift Economy [here](https://breathinginnature.com/gift-economy/).","startDate":"2026-10-03T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Humber Bay Park-West","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Humber Bay Park Road W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Wim Hof Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-wim-hof-method-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Wim Hof Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner Drop-In Pickleball – $18/1.5hrs – Register to Secure Your Spot!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316538864/","description":"🏓 **Registration & Payment (Required in Advance):**\nRSVP on Meetup does *not* guarantee your spot.\nTo play, you must register and pay in advance through our registration system.\n👉 **[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=xYXBXd6)**\n📞 Or call: 416-924-6211 ext. 0\n**Limited to 18 players.** Once full, no additional players will be admitted.\n\n***\n\n**Beginner Drop-In Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC**\n\nNew to pickleball? We’ve got the perfect session for you!\nJoin us for **Beginner Drop-In Pickleball** at the Miles Nadal JCC — a welcoming and supportive environment for those just getting started with the game. Whether you're still learning the rules or building confidence on the court, this is a great opportunity to play, practice, and meet fellow beginners.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **Event Details:**\n**Location:** 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n**Check-In:** Please check in with security and stop 