ng point]\n🚗 Transportation: Carpooling available\n💵 Cost: $30.00 [e-transfer: economatotoronto@comshalom.org]\n📝 Registration: Required by Tuesday, September 29\n\nWhat to bring:\n\nYour own light lunch\nSomething to share for the group picnic\nComfortable walking shoes and weather-appropriate clothing\nWater bottle and sunscreen\n\nSpots in the carpool are limited, so please register early to save your seat!\ni\n📞 Questions? Contact us at 647 222 9875\n\n📸 Follow us on Instagram: @shalomtoronto\n\nWe can't wait to spend the day with you! 🙌","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/catholic-hang-out-social-group/events/316671411/","isAttending":false,"isSaved":false,"maxTickets":0,"rsvpState":"JOIN_OPEN","featuredEventPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:536272302"},"displayPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:536272302"},"feeSettings":null,"group":{"__ref":"Group:34019593"},"socialProofInsights":null,"rsvps":{"__typename":"RsvpConnection","totalCount":3,"edges":[{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:457951789"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":false,"member":{"__ref":"Member:343404816"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":false,"member":{"__ref":"Member:484272319"}}}]},"series":null,"venue":{"__typename":"Venue","name":"Niagara Falls","address":"Niagara falls","city":"Toronto","state":"QC","country":"CA"}},"RecommendedEventsEdge:{\"node\":{\"id\":\"316671411\"}}":{"__typename":"RecommendedEventsEdge","node":{"__ref":"Event:316671411","id":"316671411"},"metadata":{"__typename":"SearchMetadata","recId":"cfe4c4da-3782-4bed-8e18-49dbb412c7d5","recSource":"ml-popular-events-nearby-offline"}},"PhotoInfo:517962231":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-events/","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/4/f/7/highres_517962231.jpeg","id":"517962231"},"PhotoInfo:515055409":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-events/","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/c/3/1/highres_515055409.jpeg","id":"515055409"},"Group:19532835":{"__typename":"Group","id":"19532835","name":"Inner Engineering Toronto (Isha Yoga \u0026 Meditation Classes)","urlname":"Isha-Yoga-Toronto-Free-Meditation-Classes","timezone":"America/Toronto","keyGroupPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:515055409"},"stats":{"__typename":"GroupStats","eventRatings":{"__typename":"GroupStatsEventRatings","average":4.3,"totalRatings":353}}},"Member:241600077":{"__typename":"Member","id":"241600077","name":"maha S-A","memberPhoto":null},"Event:316693725":{"__typename":"Event","id":"316693725","title":"Yogasanas: Mind-Body Alignment (Isha Hatha Yoga) Toronto","dateTime":"2026-10-03T08:00:00-04:00","description":"Click [here](https://innerengineering.sadhguru.org/toronto) to register\n\nYogasanas\n\nThe word asana literally means a posture. Out of the innumerable asanas a body can assume, 84 have been identified as Yogasanas, through which one can transform the body and mind into a possibility for ultimate well-being. Yogasanas are not exercises, but rather very subtle processes to manipulate one’s energy in a particular direction.\n\nIn an untrained state, the human body is a constant manifestation of various levels of compulsiveness. By consciously forming the body into a certain posture, one creates a conducive passage for energy flow that can elevate one’s consciousness. Yogasanas are a way of aligning the inner system and adjusting it to the celestial geometry, thereby becoming in sync with the existence and naturally achieving a chemistry of healthfulness, joyfulness, blissfulness, and above all, balance.\n\nThe practice of Yogasanas provides countless benefits including:\n\n* Relief of chronic health conditions\n* Evolution of body and mind towards a higher possibility\n* Stabilization of the body, mind, and energy system\n* Deceleration of the aging process\n\nThis is a paid program.\n\nProgram fee: CAD 300\n\nSaturday, October 3rd, 8:00 AM - 11:30 AM\nSaturday, October 3rd, 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM\nSunday, October 4th, 8:00 AM - 11:30 AM\nSunday, October 4th, 5:00 PM - 8:30 PM\n\nFor ages 18 and above, no prior knowledge of yoga is required.","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/isha-yoga-toronto-free-meditation-classes/events/316693725/","isAttending":false,"isSaved":false,"maxTickets":0,"rsvpState":"JOIN_OPEN","featuredEventPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:517962231"},"displayPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:517962231"},"feeSettings":{"__typename":"EventFeeSettings","accepts":"CASH","currency":"CAD","amount":300},"group":{"__ref":"Group:19532835"},"socialProofInsights":null,"rsvps":{"__typename":"RsvpConnection","totalCount":1,"edges":[{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:241600077"}}}]},"series":null,"venue":{"__typename":"Venue","name":"5825 Dixie Rd","address":"5825 Dixie Rd","city":"Mississauga","state":"ON","country":"ca"}},"RecommendedEventsEdge:{\"node\":{\"id\":\"316693725\"}}":{"__typename":"RecommendedEventsEdge","node":{"__ref":"Event:316693725","id":"316693725"},"metadata":{"__typename":"SearchMetadata","recId":"cfe4c4da-3782-4bed-8e18-49dbb412c7d5","recSource":"ml-popular-events-nearby-offline"}},"PhotoInfo:535962436":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-events/","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/5/c/4/highres_535962436.jpeg","id":"535962436"},"PhotoInfo:524946766":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-events/","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/a/6/e/highres_524946766.jpeg","id":"524946766"},"Group:36513000":{"__typename":"Group","id":"36513000","name":"Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club","urlname":"wildernessunion","timezone":"America/Toronto","keyGroupPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:524946766"},"stats":{"__typename":"GroupStats","eventRatings":{"__typename":"GroupStatsEventRatings","average":4.73,"totalRatings":56}}},"PhotoInfo:324278953":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","id":"324278953","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/member/9/8/2/9/highres_324278953.jpeg","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-member/"},"Member:476667737":{"__typename":"Member","id":"476667737","name":"Joshua Morgan","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:324278953"}},"PhotoInfo:321545168":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","id":"321545168","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/member/1/4/3/0/highres_321545168.jpeg","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-member/"},"Member:364108943":{"__typename":"Member","id":"364108943","name":"Wilderness Union","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:321545168"}},"PhotoInfo:323528026":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","id":"323528026","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/member/1/f/5/a/highres_323528026.jpeg","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-member/"},"Member:474700960":{"__typename":"Member","id":"474700960","name":"Salena ","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:323528026"}},"PhotoInfo:326307827":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","id":"326307827","highResUrl":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/member/6/c/b/3/highres_326307827.jpeg","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com/images/classic-member/"},"Member:217813650":{"__typename":"Member","id":"217813650","name":"Zohaib","memberPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:326307827"}},"Event:316386951":{"__typename":"Event","id":"316386951","title":"Fall Migration Birding in Toronto","dateTime":"2026-10-03T08:20:00-04:00","description":"**Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our website.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fall-birding-26)**\n\n**Toronto has some hidden natural gems, and October is when it puts on its best show.**\n\nJoin our guide Pedro Hernandez of[ Outdoor Commute](https://www.instagram.com/outdoor.commute/) for a beginner-friendly birdwatching walk through the unique Tommy Thompson Park. You do not need to know a warbler from a wren, but you probably will when the day is done. This walk is built for people who are simply curious about the birds sharing our skyline.\n\nWe’ll move slowly and stop often, learning how to identify species by shape, colour, and call, how to actually use a pair of binoculars (yours to borrow for the day), and how to make sense of field guides and birding apps you can keep using long after the trip ends.\n\nOctober is peak Fall migration in the city, with so many different birds to spot. Depending on conditions, we might spot warblers, sparrows, and thrushes moving through, along with waterfowl like northern shovelers and gadwalls resting on the water. Year-round residents including red-tailed hawks, black-capped chickadees, and northern cardinals tend to make an appearance too.\n\n**Please note that binoculars are included in the cost of the adventure and that, due to the Toronto location, transportation is not offered.**\n\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or provide feedback, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n\n**Highlights**\n**Fall Migration:** October is one of the best windows of the year to bird at the Spit, with local species and southbound migrants both moving through the park at once.\n**Professional Birder:** Pedro founded the popular birding account[ Outdoor Commute](https://www.instagram.com/outdoor.commute/) and brings a genuine, patient teaching style\n**Binoculars Included:** Every participant gets a pair of high-quality NOCS binoculars for the walk\n\n**Event cost: $60+HST (for explorer members). Register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fall-birding-26)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/316386951/","isAttending":false,"isSaved":false,"maxTickets":0,"rsvpState":"JOIN_OPEN","featuredEventPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:535962436"},"displayPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:535962436"},"feeSettings":null,"group":{"__ref":"Group:36513000"},"socialProofInsights":null,"rsvps":{"__typename":"RsvpConnection","totalCount":4,"edges":[{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:476667737"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:364108943"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":false,"member":{"__ref":"Member:474700960"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":false,"member":{"__ref":"Member:217813650"}}}]},"series":null,"venue":{"__typename":"Venue","name":"Toronto","address":"","city":"Toronto","state":"ON","country":"ca"}},"RecommendedEventsEdge:{\"node\":{\"id\":\"316386951\"}}":{"__typename":"RecommendedEventsEdge","node":{"__ref":"Event:316386951","id":"316386951"},"metadata":{"__typename":"SearchMetadata","recId":"cfe4c4da-3782-4bed-8e18-49dbb412c7d5","recSource":"ml-popular-events-nearby-offline"}},"PhotoInfo:536355549":{"__typename":"PhotoInfo","baseUrl":"https://secure-content.meetupstat